From e168736ec52e18128acd88e7e8a65df723b3982a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Oskari Rauta <oskari.rauta@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 28 Jul 2026 12:54:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 100/111] mips: xburst2: add soc-t41 machine support

Adds the Ingenic T41 as a third arm of the existing XBurst2 "SOC types"
choice, alongside SOC_T40 and SOC_X2000_V12. The machine directory comes
from the Ingenic 4.4.94 BSP as carried by gtxaspec/thingino-linux branch
ingenic-t41-4.4.94, which is the same BSP lineage as the ingenic-t40 tree
this applies to - arch/mips/xburst2/core/ is file-for-file identical
between them.

The upstream T41 tree REPLACES soc-x2000-v12 with soc-t41 in Kconfig,
Makefile and Platform. That substitution is cosmetic, so this patch adds
the T41 arm instead: no existing line is removed and SOC_T40 and
SOC_X2000_V12 keep working exactly as before.

The one shared file touched is core/include/core_base.h. It defines
INTC_IOBASE as 0x12300000, but both soc-t40 and soc-t41 define the same
name as 0x10001000 in their own soc/base.h. T40 only escapes the clash
because no T40 translation unit includes both headers; soc-t41's
pm/pm_fastboot.c does. Upstream comments the line out, which would change
T40. Guarding it with CONFIG_SOC_T41 cannot, because SOC_T40, SOC_T41 and
SOC_X2000_V12 are arms of one Kconfig choice and never coexist.

Verified: building OpenIPC's stock t40.generic.config from this tree
produces object files byte-identical to a pristine tree, apart from
__LINE__ constants shifted by the comments added here.
